The key insight from the crash: `UNKNOWN READ` at `0xfffffffffffffd68` in `D3DS::Material::Material` called from `ASE::Material::Material` during vector reallocation. The regression was introduced by commit `4d5e47a87` which changed the constructors to `= default`.

The critical issue: The `ASE::Material` copy constructor is `= default`. This copies the `D3DS::Material` base class using its defaulted copy constructor. But the `D3DS::Material` base class has a `virtual ~Material()`. When you have a virtual destructor, the defaulted copy constructor is still generated. But the `D3DS::Material` also has a user-declared copy constructor (`Material(const Material &other) = default;`). 

